==Trivia==
*The Evolved Barbarian may be based on [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samson Samson], a man that appeared in the Bible shown to have above average strength due to his longer hair.
*The word "''Barbarian''" comes from the Greek "''βάρβαρος''" (''bárbaros''), meaning foreign. Dating back to the ancient Greek times, the Greeks referred to non-Greek people as barbarians because the language they spoke sounded to Greeks like gibberish represented by the sounds "''bar..bar..;''".
*The Barbarian's Evolution resembles the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Super_Barbarian Super Barbarian] from Clash of Clans.
*The Barbarians' Evolution was one of the first [[Card Evolution|Evolutions]] to be added in the game, alongside the [[Skeletons/Evolution|Skeletons]], [[Royal Giant/Evolution|Royal Giant]], and [[Firecracker/Evolution|Firecracker]]. It is also one of the first evolved [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] to be featured in a [[Loading Screens|Loading Screen]], alongside the Skeletons, Royal Giant, and Firecracker.
*Even though the [[Cards|card]] spawns 5 Barbarians, the card render displays only 1 Barbarian.
*Unlike other troops, when the Evolved Barbarians are under their own [[Rage]] effect, their sound effects play at a lower pitch. The Evolved Barbarians under the Rage's, [[Lumberjack]]'s, or the [[Lumberjack/Evolution|Evolved Lumberjack]]'s effects will play higher pitched sounds as normal.
**Along with the [[Knight/Evolution|Knight]] and [[Lumberjack/Evolution|Lumberjack]], he is one of the Evolutions voice acted by [https://www.imdb.com/name/nm1423395/ John Mondelli].
*The Barbarian's Evolution is featured on the card render of the [[Zap/Evolution|Zap's Evolution]].
*It is said that Barbarians cannot function without their swords. This is referenced a few times:
**The Duelist [[Battle Banners|Decoration]] saying "''Swords. Barbarians don't enter the Arena without them!''"
**The [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Raged_Barbarian Raged Barbarian]'s description in Clash of Clans which says "''Why is he so angry, speedy, and vicious? Nobody's brave enough to ask. Maybe it's because he can't find his sword?''"
**In the Clash-A-Rama episode "[https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/%22Ballad_of_the_Barbarian%22 Ballad of the Barbarian]", a Barbarian was depressed because he lost his sword.
*There is a [[Loading Screen Hints|Loading Screen Hint]] that says: "''Don't feed Barbarian after midnight.''" This is a reference to [https://gremlins.fandom.com/wiki/Gremlins_Wiki Gremlins].
*The Barbarians' Evolution is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].
*Before the Barbarians' Evolution's release, the Evolved Barbarians' boost was decreased to 50% (from 150%).

